{"title":"Mock AIME I 2015 Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Rigorous_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rigorous Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Corrected_Solution_and_Answer\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Corrected Solution and Answer</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Original_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Original Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2015_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d2ee4cd42e5edb7ec72c8281f599b6d6db2f23c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_x 3y = \\tfrac{20}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"93\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f033b96216c7a4e03f2e0c7ee3bb15b6c3d198dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{3x}y=\\tfrac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"84\" height=\"21\" />.  The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85812706e54de2020e934734f87a5eb04a0b772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{3x}3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f43eacde9585e1bbb12e8030dd1486db61d2c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive relatively prime integers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rigorous_Solution\">Rigorous Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2015_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Rigorous Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin with the second statement that \\( \\log_{3x}(y)=2/3 \\). Through the definition of logarithms, this is equivalent to \\( (3x)^{2/3} = y \\), or \\( \\sqrt[3]{9x^2} = y \\).\n</p><p>We then see that the first equation, through the definition of logarithms, is equivalent to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4d252c6a5254ad0e0b08ad1f84cf8bbc4ac6542.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_x(3y)=\\frac{20}{13} \\Rightarrow x^{20/13} = 3y\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa527bb962e908c2899a89aac9c34d569619b88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{using the definition of } y\\text{,}\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e4ad1950c02af31ea9f6d11eeb0621e687c75a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{20/13} = 3(\\sqrt[3]{9x^2})\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"22\" />\nCubing both sides achieves\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff9491d955335411f80ed76aaaceaf1b9c0b740.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{60/13} = (3^5)(x^2)\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"21\" />\nDividing by 2 achieves\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a2d6328a2a1ba0221d9484347523ea898b2876c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{34/13} = (3^5)\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" />\nRaising both sides to the power of 13/34,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f419dbbf928b0763ff043bcc7676fb6c10b36d61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 3^{65/34}\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />\nThrough the definition of y,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/f/d5fb9dbcccd68053b799d7f281f191501ad63bdc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(3x)^{2/3} = y\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5a97b64ab91c0520650fdb1705f4521ac1fbc8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(3^{99/34})^{2/3} = y\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd252f23fa98c0a4442cc709275f7c518e9a370.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3^{33/17} = y\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>To evaluate \\( \\log_{3x}(3y) \\), we see that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcbbe226a153c5b5fffdb26db00666966e1a26d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{3^{99/34}}(3^{50/17})\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>In which we use two useful logarithmic properties\n</p><p>- \\( \\log_{a^n}(b)=\\frac{1}{n}\\log_a(b) \\)\n</p><p>- \\( \\log_a(b^n)=n\\log_a(b) \\)\n</p><p>So, applying that here, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcbbe226a153c5b5fffdb26db00666966e1a26d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{3^{99/34}}(3^{50/17})\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536576b863867495dbe4e415e8b6da10551e4b2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{99}{34} \\cdot \\log_{3}(3^{50/17})\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/656cb4ad6d66c870b4cecaa7eaef2ec500219056.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{99}{34} \\cdot \\frac{50}{17} \\log_3(3)\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94e548a00c9e86ce8cf35439dcd09722e606895a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{100}{99}\\]\" width=\"27\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>This is in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/508eff1eb45608456e0c7271a12dc5743710112a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = 100 + 99 = \\boxed{199}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"196\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Corrected_Solution_and_Answer\">Corrected Solution and Answer</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2015_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Corrected Solution and Answer\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the logarithmic identity  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa971ae2777904bf9906e43d1e307bbc6bc15bf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_q p = \\frac{log_r p}{log_r q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"113\" height=\"43\" /> to expand the assumptions to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bd24b673abbc33178d504ce06261fc43e1af706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_x 3y = \\frac{log_3 3y}{log_3 x}  = \\frac{1+log_3 y}{log_3 x} = \\frac{20}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"275\" height=\"41\" />  \n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8febf8aebb1260cafd7763906d4ded88380acff0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{3x} y = \\frac{log_3 y}{log_3 3x}  = \\frac{log_3 y}{1+log_3 x} = \\frac{2}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"271\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Solve for the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a99464fc4a6d82a4e4d70c67595ae296813d236a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_3 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/8/28839d7491409d3884d896f71db6158099a1fd24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_3 y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> which are respectively <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05afaa2b5d1b556173be95edd7db8e306e1cae25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{65}{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/775cbb514f898f5b0b15b6d03e8ba9eb304e58cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{33}{17}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The sought ratio is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d5abb387a74aeafc6467f64ca050998efc3d24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{3x} 3y = \\frac{log_3 3y}{log_3 3x}  = \\frac{1+log_3 y}{1+log_3 x} = \\frac{1+\\tfrac{33}{17}}{1+\\tfrac{65}{34}} = \\frac{100}{99}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"375\" height=\"47\" /> \n</p><p>The answer then is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7c1bec48d3210d75c8ef5408e8b322b11e1f45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100+99=\\boxed{199}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>Solution by D. Adrian Tanner\n(Original solution and answer below)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Original_Solution\">Original Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2015_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Original Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By rearranging the values, it is possible to attain an \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a197330a691e15ec6633db4b8c4c95c3203a02bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= 3^ {65/17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdc18649b4f8bbc45dc737c8091736bf99fba825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y= 3^ {33/17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, a/b is     equal to 25/61,  so 25+41= 061\n</p><p>Ignore the original solution as it is incorrect - blunderbro\nSolution at the top checked by blunderbro\nNote: It is correct, original one was the first one posted but was incorrect.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017212239\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 187/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6761/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13833:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017212239 and revision id 270505. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}